Scope and third-party components

The MIT licence above covers the Multi-LoRA system and evaluation scripts written
for this repository, i.e. `mul_lora_systems/`, `evaluate_official.py` and `lora/`.

`YAOGAN_CHAT-main/` is the demo web system (React front-end + FastAPI back-end)
shipped alongside the model code. It carries no licence file of its own and its
upstream authorship is not recorded here, so please confirm its terms before
re-licensing or redistributing that sub-directory.

The following files are upstream model code and keep their original licences and
copyright headers; they are redistributed here so the checkpoint can be loaded
with `trust_remote_code=True`:

- `modeling_fm9g.py`, `configuration_fm9g.py`, `tokenization_fm9g.py`,
  `modeling_fm9gv.py`, `image_processing_fm9gv.py`, `processing_fm9gv.py`,
  `tokenization_fm9gv_fast.py` - derived from the "NineGrids" (FM9G / 九章文澜)
  remote-sensing multimodal model implementation, which itself is based on the
  HuggingFace LLaMA implementation (Apache License 2.0).
- `modeling_navit_siglip.py` - NaViT SigLIP vision encoder (InternLM/Shell-Camel
  lineage, Apache License 2.0).
- `resampler.py` - Copyright (c) Alibaba Cloud, Qwen-VL style resampler.
- `tokenizer.json`, `tokenizer.model`, `tokenizer_config.json`,
  `special_tokens_map.json`, `added_tokens.json`, `config.json`,
  `preprocessor_config.json` - tokenizer / processor assets shipped with the
  official checkpoint.

The base model weights (`pytorch_model.bin`, not stored in this repository) are
distributed separately by the NineGrids team under their own licence terms - check
the upstream model card before any redistribution or commercial use.
